{"content":[{"c":["MAADIAH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Head of a priestly family who returned to Jerusalem after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.5","r":"Neh.12.5","rawR":"Neh.12.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.5","value":"Neh.12.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:5"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg) and whose house was headed by Piltai in the next generation during the days of Joiakim the high priest. He is called Moadiah in v ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.17","r":"Neh.12.17","rawR":"Neh.12.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.17","value":"Neh.12.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"17"},". He is perhaps identifiable with the priest Maaziah, who set his seal on Ezra’s covenant (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.8","r":"Neh.10.8","rawR":"Neh.10.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.8","value":"Neh.10.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Maadiah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Neh 12:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.5","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.5","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.5"},{"anchorText":"17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.17","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.17","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.17"},{"anchorText":"10:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.8","rawQueryValue":"Neh.10.8","sourceRefExact":"Neh.10.8"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b1f80cc594d5dfb54e5e8cd2ced857e845611bd44474196abefe5fa440fcd9d7","sourceItemName":"Maadiah","sourceItemOrder":5,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Maadiah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Maadiah*","title":"Maadiah*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}